{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You shall release it.</b> The remission of debts, as it says: וְזֶה דְּבַר הַשְּׁמִטָּה, שָׁמוֹט כָּל בַּעַל מַשֵּׁה יָדוֹ (Deuteronomy 15:2)." "<b>And you shall leave it, and the needy of your people shall eat.</b> In the sabbatical year of the land the poor also eat." "<b>And what remains.</b> What belongs to the poor." "<b>The beasts of the field shall eat.</b> The poor take precedence, as the Sages said: food fit for human consumption is forbidden to feed to dogs (Ta'anit 20b)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:57.485984678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}